Package: path2path
Type: Package
Title: Directional Pathway-by-Pathway Interaction Maps from
        Genome-Scale Perturb-Seq
Version: 0.99.2
Authors@R: person("Jun", "Li", email = "jun.li@nd.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4353-5761"))
Description: Builds a directional pathway-by-pathway interaction map from
    genome-scale Perturb-seq differential-expression statistics by two
    stacked runs of preranked gene set enrichment analysis: once per
    perturbation over genes, then once per readout pathway over
    perturbations. Entry (j,k) of the resulting matrix measures whether
    perturbations targeting pathway j's members produce a coordinated
    transcriptional response in pathway k. The package includes target
    exclusion, effective-size filters, overlap masking, Stage 2 p-values
    with false-discovery-rate control, and a whole-pipeline permutation
    calibration with generalized-Pareto tail estimation.
